// DECEMBER 10 — THE WISH
// Separate feedback version. Existing scene4.yarn and Unity scenes are unchanged.
// This is one uninterrupted in-game cutscene in the Dorm; the player makes no choice here.
// Continue from Dec10_Rooftop_Exit / Dec10_Dorm_Return when the new flow is wired.
// UI SETUP: Add StorySplashOverlay to an active image under the Dorm HUD, behind BubbleRoot.
// Assign cutscene_prologue_2a once as Character Placeholder for all four portraits.
// Calendar Normal and Calendar Circled may stay empty: the overlay shows black placeholders.
// ART TODO: Dedicated Kirana, Lila, Dira, Fal portraits; normal and circled calendar close-ups.
// ANIMATION TODO: Anin flinches, climbs into bed, sleeps with eyes open, then closes them.
// CAMERA TODO: Close in on the circled calendar after Anin shuts her eyes.
// STORY TODO: Replace the final placeholder with the new loop-start transition when written.

title: Dec10_Wish_Dorm
tags: december10 dorm night wish testing
---
// Anin enters alone. The Dorm door opens, she walks in, and it closes.
// Stage Anin at the doorway before this node starts. Tune X positions tomorrow.
<<hide "Kirana">>
<<open_door "Dorm">>
<<move_character "Anin" -3.4 3 "walk">>
<<close_door "Dorm">>
Anin: These last few days at school have been so damn fun.
Anin: Seeing my friends without having to study for once.
Anin: Just hanging out, talking, making one last batch of memories together.

// The group illustration is a placeholder for Kirana's portrait.
<<story_splash "kirana">>
Anin: Kirana.
Anin: My best friend and my roommate.
Anin: We've shared a room since our first year here.
Anin: Back then, we weren't even that close. We fought about something almost every day.
Anin: Like when my alarm went off, I'd snooze it and go right back to sleep. Again and again.
Anin: She said I had no discipline. Can you believe her?
Anin: That's our group leader for you. Always looking out for us.
Anin: Her parents have already planned her whole life after school. She's pretty much set.

// The same group illustration temporarily stands in for Lila's portrait.
<<story_splash "lila">>
Anin: Lila. The loud one.
Anin: When she's not around, you can feel how quiet everything gets.
Anin: Loud and dumb, too.
Anin: She once fell for a delivery scam because someone said her package had arrived four hours after she ordered it.
Anin: Girl, you ordered from another island. Four hours? At least be suspicious.
Anin: She's the type to believe any gossip she hears.
Anin: But then again, even someone as dumb as her knows where she's headed.
Anin: Journalism. With her camera skills and how she can make friends with anyone, she's basically set for life.

// The same group illustration temporarily stands in for Dira's portrait.
<<story_splash "dira">>
Anin: Dira.
Anin: The only sane one in our group.
Anin: She's honestly perfect. Smart, calm, kind.
Anin: Sometimes I feel bad that she hangs out with disasters like us.
Anin: Maybe that's why our group has lasted, though. We're all so different.
Anin: And like the others, she knows where she's going. Probably overprepared, honestly.

// The same group illustration temporarily stands in for Fal's portrait.
<<story_splash "fal">>
Anin: Fal.
Anin: Of all the boys I've met at this school, he seems... different.
Anin: It's like we understand each other really well.
Anin: Whenever one of us needs something, the other one is there.
Anin: He's pretty amazing, isn't he?
Anin: But lately he's seemed down. I wonder what happened.
<<story_splash_end>>

// Anin walks to the far-left window. Keep the normal dialogue bubble over her.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" -10 3 "walk">>
Anin: How do they all know what they want to do after school?
Anin: All I wanted was to keep enjoying high school forever.
Anin: And look where that got me. I still have no fucking clue what I want to be. Graduation's tomorrow. Shit, I'm too late.
Anin: I'm... scared.
// Anin steps back and flinches. The flinch animation needs art later.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" -9 2 "walk">>
Anin: I'm... scared to move on with my life.
Anin: I want to go back...
Anin: Go back and rewind the time I have with my friends.
Anin: I don't want to lose them.
Anin: And I don't want to lose my future, either.

// FLASHBACK: Literal fade in/out and a brief image of Lila telling the myth.
// The current fade command uses the existing circle transition as a temporary visual.
// The centered group art is a temporary still for the memory; replace it with the actual scene later.
// memory_montage plays the existing memory transition sounds.
<<fade>>
<<memory_montage true>>
<<story_splash "lila">>
Lila: It's an old school myth. Circle today's date on a calendar, make a wish before midnight, and you'll wake up to the same day again.
<<story_splash_end>>
<<memory_montage false>>
<<fade>>
Anin: ...

// Anin approaches the calendar. Tune the X destination to the calendar prop tomorrow.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" 3 3 "walk">>
<<story_splash "calendar_normal">>
Anin: Well... nothing to lose, I guess.
// This plays the existing paper and writing sounds. Calendar visuals are placeholders.
<<edit_calendar>>
<<story_splash "calendar_circled">>
Anin: Me? Believing one of Lila's rumors? I must be really desperate, huh?
<<story_splash_end>>

// Anin walks to bed, climbs in, and lies awake. All three pose beats need animation.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Anin" -5 3 "walk">>
<<delay 0.5>>
// Sleep pose: eyes open.
<<dialogue_speed 18>>
Anin: Thank you...
Anin: And goodbye, everyone...
<<dialogue_speed 0>>
// Sleep pose: eyes close. Camera closes in on the circled calendar.
<<story_splash "calendar_circled">>
<<sfx "hard_reset">>
// LOOP TRANSITION PLACEHOLDER: Do not call the old hard_reset; it loads the old story.
// End this feedback draft here until the new loop-start Yarn exists.
===
